# Integration pages — layout language

Applies to `/integrations/shopify` and `/integrations/commercetools`.

Homepage, solutions, and industry pages have their own rules. Integrations reuse the same section rhythm and shared patterns, with two hard constraints:

1. Keep the hero ownership split (`OwnershipDiagram`: platform keeps vs CubeCom adds).
2. Stay candid about maturity — “early access”, “intended pattern”, “not an App Store / marketplace connector yet.” Do not visually imply a finished marketplace connector.

## Canonical skeleton

```text
Hero + ownership split
→ Problem / boundary
→ Full-width integration visual
→ Dark mechanism
→ Capabilities
→ Real integration proof
→ Outcomes
→ Bridge + FAQ
→ Final CTA
```

## Proof type

- **Shopify:** believable PDP configuration → Shopify cart line (candid handoff note).
- **commercetools:** selection → resolve → commercetools cart projection (request/response / architecture proof). Prefer depth over packaging claims.

## Shared primitives

`SolutionHero`, `OwnershipDiagram`, `ProblemCompare`, `FullWidthVisual`, `SignatureMechanism`, `EditorialColumns`, proof components, `OutcomeGrid`, `SolutionBridge`, `SeoFaq`, `SeoCta`, `@repo/ui`.

If a dedicated integration visual asset is missing, keep a blank `MediaSlot` via `FullWidthVisual` — never invent HTML/CSS marketplace chrome.
